  <!-- ⚠️ STUB — PREMISES NOT YET VERIFIED. Author with /task-create. Task 106 rewrote this region, so
       any line number below is already suspect. See notes/task-accuracy-audit-2026-09-18.md. -->

  <owner-decision date="2026-09-18">"When access is renewed the user should have the same level as previous access period." A renewal must NOT lower the effective level; the prior period's level carries forward rather than the requested level overwriting it.</owner-decision>

  <prompt>The read path composes effective access as `GroupBy(root).Max(level)` over active, unexpired rows. The write path's `CollapseDuplicatesAsync` writes the REQUESTED level to the survivor and deactivates every other row. So a re-grant at ViewOnly over a key holding a FullAccess duplicate reduces effective access from FullAccess to ViewOnly — on a request whose caller may have meant only to renew. This is pre-existing (task 010 convergence semantics); task 106 provably does not change level outcomes, because the requested level is written to whichever row is elected.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external grant lifecycle.</role>
  <goal>A renewal preserves the previous period's effective level, while an explicit level change — including a DOWNGRADE — still applies exactly as requested.</goal>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The renewal-vs-explicit-change discriminator is a CONTRACT decision. If it cannot be made without a request-shape change (a new field, a new route, or a changed meaning for an existing one), STOP and escalate with options rather than inferring intent from the payload.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-18">🔴 The rule CANNOT be implemented as "always take `max(requested, existing)`" — that makes downgrades impossible. Task 063's `share-user` path exists to set a system user to View Only, and the pre-merge real-Dataverse DOWNGRADE check (task 063 notes §9.4) is about exactly that working. An explicit downgrade MUST remain possible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="audit 2026-09-18">⚠️ Constrain task **099** as part of this: 099 is the renewal UI and its acceptance criteria say nothing about level, so as specified it would present a date picker while the server silently changed the level. Check task **101**'s views too.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Response contract: status codes and reasonCodes unchanged; needing a new one is an escalation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-023. Related: tasks 010, 023, 063, 097, 098, 099, 101, 106.</notes>
</task>
